<title>SOUTH KOREA: Trigem, ALEX limit-down.</title>
<headline>Trigem, ALEX limit-down.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of South Korea's Trigem Computer and ALEX Computer went limit-down on Wednesday on rumours of financial trouble, brokers said.</p>
<p>Trigem fell 2,200 won to its daily lower limit of 25,800 and ALEX dropped 3,500 won to 41,200.</p>
<p>&quot;The speculation on financial problems seems to be stemming from sluggish personal computer sales,&quot; said Koh Soon-shik, a broker at LG Securities.</p>
<p>Officials at the companies said the rumours were groundless.</p>
<p>Daewoo Telecom, a unit of Daewoo Group, also dropped 600 won to 8,400. It briefly hit its limit-down of 8,280.</p>
<p>Government figures showing recent personal computer sales were not immediately available.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
